t_uuid":"e1fd14d6-6501-4ead-b35f-d2e0a896be12","position":{"commit_sha":"ecb9f50d7b64f65d7a385aa8e3757a6f8693d670","position":"1794872181946034029-e1fd14d6-6501-4ead-b35f-d2e0a896be12"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e5c48952e80fdb7f503270399c237fc97b6290e038d7f99000bb17d555f623e2","event_uuid":"6ad32c6e-d507-459d-af62-9d7d7f98206e","position":{"commit_sha":"3befd99d91e16498a4b8dd254132ca2da5382851","position":"1794872528719373403-6ad32c6e-d507-459d-af62-9d7d7f98206e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"01298935a9bd8e5c094811078cc76a82476cbec74f70eda7d09aca8bc568485a","event_uuid":"55ccd255-68a4-4a0b-8fc0-e5615c34d8fe","position":{"commit_sha":"1195f4cb9e790676c86852c600d151eb525b4f10","position":"1794873098736927700-55ccd255-68a4-4a0b-8fc0-e5615c34d8fe"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Retained UNCHANGED in the 2026-08-29 epic re-scope. This forced remote-override is **lever-agnostic**: it enforces the C3 stale-clone override that makes ANY below-horizon reclamation safe, and is directly required by the new S1 commit/tree-collapse rewrite (not just `.retired` GC). No scope change needed. See epic 536b comment 'Child-roster re-scope'.","timestamp":1788046442143427257},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress: plan-review certified (pipeline engine, verified_at b4e0d01b649); claimed. Implemented TDD on branch aff9-stale-clone-override (commit 0c4709684bf): new src/rebar/_store/stale_override.py, compat epoch_lineage + remote_epoch_supersedes_local + superseding_record, sync._do_reconverge hook, docs/concurrency.md reconnect protocol, tests/unit/test_stale_clone_override.py (9 tests, RED then green). make lint/typecheck green, mechanism + complexity ratchets exit 0. make verify running before Gerrit push. Side finding filed: shifty-genocidal-bat (gate_status stayed \"running\" ~60 min after the review signed).","timestamp":1794858530986644312},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify on 0c4709684bff (3 h wall under heavy host contention): 21287 passed, 7 failed + 2 errors, all attributed outside this change — 3 are sandbox denials of AF_UNIX/multiprocessing semaphores (test_network_guard_local_ipc x2, test_atomic_completion_close two-process test; all 7 pass when rerun outside the agent sandbox), and 6 are host-load timeouts (observability.sh 60 s subprocess timeouts x4, git rev-parse 5 s timeout x2; all pass when rerun in isolation). Pushed as Gerrit change 3405 (hashtag rebar-session-3d705fec); awaiting LLM-Review and Verified.","timestamp":1794869533798591224}],"created_at":1787594790468650001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dc60f473-413f-4518-a0cc-4a46ccbcf02e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"866f-440c-3686-42df"},{"link_uuid":"ecb264f4-6475-4b61-bf95-c1f007e3dd7c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"607f-065a-7c98-48e7"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nADR 0106 §5 (`docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md:114-124`) requires that a clone whose last convergence predates the N-day reclaim horizon OVERRIDE its local `tickets` with the remote on reconnect, instead of reintroducing pre-collapse history. Today nothing implements that: after a publish-swap every clone's local `tickets` shares no commit with the rewritten remote, and `sync._do_reconverge` (`src/rebar/_store/sync.py:94`, refusal at `:111-121`) refuses to merge unrelated histories that carry ticket events and logs `DIVERGED`. Such a clone stays wedged forever, its writes are refused by `freshness.write_blocking_divergence`, and a manual repair risks the resurrection (re-merging reclaimed events) that the horizon exists to prevent. This story closes that hole so the S2 publish-swap and S3 dry-run can rely on enforced, not probabilistic, convergence (epic C3).\n\n## Approach\n\nReuse the existing store-epoch guard rather than invent a new marker. `.store-compat.json` already carries an optional opaque `epoch` and `compat.store_epoch_problem` (`src/rebar/_store/compat.py:198`) already refuses unions across differing epochs (commit `019e32e03d1`, ticket ac32), but nothing yet stamps or interprets a successor epoch. A reclaimed baseline is identified by a remote record whose `epoch` differs from the local one AND whose new `epoch_lineage` list names the local epoch (JSON `null` stands for the pre-epoch/absent record). That lineage is the proof that the remote is a rewrite of THIS store, not an unrelated store, so unrelated stores keep today's refusal.\n\nOn reconverge, when HEAD and the remote share no merge-base and the remote epoch supersedes the local one, a new module `src/rebar/_store/stale_override.py` runs under the write lock `_do_reconverge` already holds:\n\n1. **Local-only events.** Parse event filenames per the I2 contract (`{ts}-{uuid}-{TYPE}.json`, optional `.retired`; `docs/event-schema.md:14-29`). A local event is *unpushed* iff its uuid appears nowhere on the remote tip — not as a file under the ticket dir (any suffix), and not in any remote SNAPSHOT's `data.source_event_uuids` for that ticket (`docs/event-schema.md:54`). Local SNAPSHOT events are derived state and are never replayed. This is the no-resurrection rule: anything the remote folded or retired is known to it and is not re-added.\n2. **Stale vs fresh.** The clone is *stale* iff its oldest unpushed event's `ts` is older than `now − [reclaim].horizon_days` (`config.reclaim_horizon_days`, `src/rebar/config.py:288`). Because every write auto-pushes (I5), the oldest unpushed write bounds the clone's last convergence.\n3. **Backup, then override.** Point `refs/rebar/stale-override/<utc-stamp>` at the old local HEAD (local only, never pushed), then `reset --hard` to the pinned remote commit.\n4. **Fresh clones replay; stale clones do not.** A fresh clone re-adds its unpushed event files byte-identically (`.retired` suffix stripped) in ONE local commit on top of the remote, which the normal push path then delivers. A stale clone replays nothing and logs a WARNING naming the backup ref and the discarded event count — the accepted residual loss in ADR 0106 §5.\n\n`compat.py` gains `epoch_lineage` parsing (malformed lineage fails closed like a malformed `epoch`), a `remote_epoch_supersedes_local(tracker, remote_commit)` predicate, and a pure `superseding_record(record, new_epoch)` that S2's publish-swap will use to stamp the rewritten baseline. `write_compat_record` (`compat.py:347`) preserves `epoch_lineage` just as it already preserves `epoch`. No config key, env var, or feature flag is added; the horizon key already exists.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_store/stale_override.py` (new): local-only event detection, stale classification, backup ref, override, fresh replay.\n- `src/rebar/_store/compat.py`: `epoch_lineage` parse, supersedes predicate, `superseding_record`, lineage-preserving write.\n- `src/rebar/_store/sync.py`: in `_do_reconverge`'s unrelated-history branch, call the override when the remote supersedes; otherwise keep the existing refusal unchanged.\n- `tests/unit/test_stale_clone_override.py` (new).\n- `docs/concurrency.md`: document the reconnect protocol under \"Inbound — background sync\".\n\n## Testing\n\nTDD, red first, using throwaway `git init` remotes and clones under `tmp_path` (never the live tracker). The fixture builds a store, clones it, then rewrites the remote into a parentless baseline carrying a superseding epoch record.\n\n- Happy path, stale: a clone whose only unpushed event is older than the horizon is overridden — HEAD equals the remote, the event file is gone, the backup ref holds the old HEAD.\n- Happy path, fresh: a clone with an unpushed event inside the horizon ends on a commit whose parent is the remote tip and which adds exactly that event file.\n- No resurrection: a local event that the remote retired (`.retired`) or folded (listed in a remote SNAPSHOT's `source_event_uuids`) is NOT replayed.\n- Failure/edge: an unrelated remote (different epoch, lineage not naming the local epoch) and a remote with a malformed `epoch_lineage` both still refuse with `DIVERGED`, leaving local HEAD untouched; a clone with no unpushed events simply resets to the remote with nothing replayed.\n- `write_compat_record` round-trips `epoch_lineage`; `superseding_record` appends the old epoch (or `null`) to the lineage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A simulated >N-day-stale clone reconverging against a superseding-epoch rewritten remote is overridden, not merged: HEAD equals the remote commit, no local-only event survives in the tree, and `refs/rebar/stale-override/*` points at the old HEAD — checked by `tests/unit/test_stale_clone_override.py`.\n  - evidence: `test_stale_clone_is_overridden_not_merged` passes on merged commit 9099c548247 (Gerrit change 3405).\n- [x] A fresh (<N-day) clone's unpushed events are replayed in one commit on top of the remote, and retired or SNAPSHOT-folded events are not replayed — checked by the same test module.\n  - evidence: `test_fresh_clone_replays_unpushed_events_on_top_of_remote` and `test_retired_or_folded_events_are_not_resurrected` pass.\n- [x] Unrelated or malformed-lineage remotes keep the existing `DIVERGED` refusal with local HEAD unchanged — checked by the same test module.\n  - evidence: `test_unproven_rewrites_keep_the_diverged_refusal` (unrelated, malformed and missing lineage) passes.\n- [x] `docs/concurrency.md` documents the reconnect protocol (lineage proof, stale classification, backup ref, accepted loss).\n  - evidence: paragraph \"Reconnect after a history reclaim (ADR 0106 §5)\" plus the updated pseudocode in \"Inbound — background sync\".\n- [x] `make verify` passes; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exit 0.\n  - evidence: both ratchets exit 0. Local `make verify` ran 21287 passed; its 9 non-passing tests were all reproduced as environmental (3 agent-sandbox IPC denials that pass outside the sandbox, 6 host-load timeouts that pass in isolation). CI `Verified +1` on change 3405 runs the same pytest selections and passed.\n- [x] [non-codebase] No live tickets store or the shared tickets remote branch is rewritten, reset, or force-pushed by this story; all evidence comes from throwaway pytest temporary repositories.\n  provenance: environment=developer-workstation-worktree; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=static-analysis — the merged change adds library code and unit tests whose git mutations all target tmp_path repositories, and no reclaim, swap or reset was executed against any real store.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/stale_override.py","reason":"New: local-only event detection, stale classification, backup ref, forced override, fresh-clone replay."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/compat.py","reason":"epoch_lineage parsing, remote_epoch_supersedes_local predicate, superseding_record, lineage-preserving write_compat_record."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/sync.py","reason":"_do_reconverge unrelated-history branch calls the override when the remote epoch supersedes the local one."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_stale_clone_override.py","reason":"RED-first coverage of stale override, fresh replay, no-resurrection, and refusal paths."},{"path":"docs/concurrency.md","reason":"Document the stale-clone reconnect protocol."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","866f-440c-3686-42df"],["parent","536b-8930-b922-4063"],["relates_to","607f-065a-7c98-48e7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","parent_status_uuid":"d88bd7c7-aa0a-4c40-a68f-17ffcad960c8","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"aff9-1252-ad21-4695","ticket_type":"story","title":"Stale-clone detection + forced remote-override on reconnect","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1ea35c71-fab0-4c41-896b-0eb9ed737da1","8453f881-6885-437d-bc25-c13c53a51102","f50d178a-a6eb-4a74-a7fe-85cc06f2be4c","012616cd-cc1f-46b3-a430-0dca6dc545ac","d88bd7c7-aa0a-4c40-a68f-17ffcad960c8","54e335d0-a762-43fd-9f6d-3dad5a3a11d7","c9e5d0aa-b0e0-41b6-b76a-bd04576d5253","44971b15-7f7a-43ff-b0c9-e23d8ff6ee1a","19e8b421-7df7-4e87-a9a2-6726e5fae60b","4d23678c-e543-4b2e-a1c5-97e85f72626b","ea0fb45c-c6f5-4b95-ac0d-2c505bfebf38","ecb264f4-6475-4b61-bf95-c1f007e3dd7c","e1fd14d6-6501-4ead-b35f-d2e0a896be12","6ad32c6e-d507-459d-af62-9d7d7f98206e","55ccd255-68a4-4a0b-8fc0-e5615c34d8fe"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794873098736927701,"uuid":"5ad66c02-050b-4070-8953-84202bc0ff8f"}